# Exact source successor views

This is a test-source compatibility layer, not a supervisor runtime, trust
enrollment or release admission API. It verifies five complete current files
before applying fixed inverse edits and verifying their complete predecessors.
Unknown paths pass through unchanged; old, partially installed or otherwise
modified bytes at a known path refuse. Only the immutable edit description is
cached, never a current observation. No new Git or filesystem reads occur in
the projection.

The three authority/kernel files map producer `958b3135` to `c91068bf`; COMPAT
maps the terminal GET-owner rollback `a67a5299` to `3c52c0aa`; the registry maps
`958b3135` to `3c52c0aa`. Full commit IDs and both complete canonical SHA256 values
are in `rules.json`. The edits cover the previously measured fresh-fstat leaves,
test-only attribution/rejected experiments, thirteen manual gate registrations,
and the diagnostic TLS/allocation/rollback compatibility entries. They do not
approve those changes as product performance candidates.

`generate.py` reconstructs the description from those fixed Git commits with
replacement objects disabled. With no arguments it checks the existing file;
`--write` creates it exclusively and refuses to overwrite it. It never uses HEAD,
the index or worktree observations to authorize new expected values. SHA256
`61d3e1941cdae497600592a49af0487e4cf545573ba3f091add173110b560cda`
is separately pinned in the Rust reader. Keep this file LF on every platform.

The existing owned-case layer already accounts for the held-launcher test's
three-line addition. It is deliberately absent from this new five-path scope.
The old IO reader, inventory ledgers, all twenty artifact tests, primitive
reviewed-byte predicates and original authority assertions remain unchanged.
The two historical entry points now require the successor before running their
old checks. Their raw primitive `accepts` functions still describe the old phase;
they are not standalone current-source approval APIs.

Run the producer check and the dedicated test target:

```text
python tools/source-successor-view-074/generate.py
cargo test --offline --locked -p xtask --test source_successor_view_074 --test diagnostic_artifact_fixture_074 -- --test-threads=4
```

The tests compare both ends against independent fixed Git producers, exercise
missing/duplicate/partial/stale/wrong-path/extra-body mutations, preserve the
exact old gate bodies except their named entry edits, and repeat observations
after a success. This proves source preservation for those edits. It does not
prove arbitrary semantic equivalence of the runtime, race freedom, Linux
behavior, numerical improvements or the full package gate.
